## Single Finger Touch Dragging

By default, Single Finger Touch Drag events are handled like mouse drag events. To change the input handling behavior of these events, use `touch.dragAction`.

{% chartExampleRunner
    title="Single Finger Touch Dragging"
    name="single-finger-touch-dragging"
    type="generated"
    options={ "enterprise": true }
/%}

```ts
touch: {
    dragAction: 'none',
}
```

In this example:

-   `dragAction: 'none'` disables Single Finger input handling, scrolling the page.
-   `dragAction: 'drag'` emulates mouse dragging, updating the view's pan.
-   `dragAction: 'hover'` emulates mouse movements, updating the tooltip & highlight.

